# Slice 334 (Codex check of 334): every actual of a receiver is received by its formal before the next actual is
# evaluated. `fn: bad 7 int touch()` binds the form [name, args, return, code]; args receives 7, no Structure, so the
# receiver is refused there (the interpreter answers 5; native and forced code fail there) before touch(), the body's
# actual, is evaluated: touch() never runs, so Box\hits stays 0 (before 0; after never computed). The dump prints the
# data of touch as written, so the finally of the root copies Box\hits into at_end after the refusal: at_end is 0 here,
# and 1 with `fn: ok (int: a) int touch()`, where touch() is evaluated first and the refusal comes later.
# Plan M11 5v: the declaration of the ordinary Structure Box lives in the data part of touch, the only method that uses
# it; the root reads Box by the path touch\data\Box and keeps the places, the finally and the refused receiver.
fn: touch () int (
    Box:
        int: hits 0
)
    Box\hits := Box\hits + 1
    return: 3
int: at_end 9
finally:
    at_end := touch\data\Box\hits
int: before touch\data\Box\hits
fn: bad 7 int touch()
int: after touch\data\Box\hits
